(OPERATION HIMALAYAN SHIELD - OPERATION ORDER 07/2026) Tj
T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Reference: Northern Command Contingency Plan HS-2026. Time Zone Used Throughout the Order:) Tj
T*
(INDIA STANDARD TIME \(IST\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Task Organisation. 14 Mountain Brigade \(main effort\), reinforced by one mechanised infantry) Tj
T*
(battalion, one medium artillery regiment \(155mm\), one combat engineer company, and one army) Tj
T*
(aviation flight \(utility and reconnaissance\). 27 Signals Regiment provides area communications.) Tj
T*
(Attached: one field surgical team and one forward logistics element.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. SITUATION.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(a. Enemy Forces. Opposing formations are assessed to hold prepared defensive positions along) Tj
T*
(the northern approaches to the Leh sector at a strength of approximately two reinforced) Tj
T*
(battalions, supported by dug-in anti-tank guided missile teams and dispersed mortar sections.) Tj
T*
(Enemy air activity is assessed as limited to unmanned reconnaissance. Most likely enemy course) Tj
T*
(of action is a mobile defence oriented on the two principal valley roads, trading space for) Tj
T*
(time while attempting to canalise our advance into pre-registered artillery engagement areas.) Tj
T*
(Most dangerous course of action is a spoiling attack against our assembly areas during the) Tj
T*
(hours of darkness preceding H-Hour.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(b. Friendly Forces. 3 Infantry Division continues the defence of the eastern sector and) Tj
T*
(protects the right flank of this brigade. Corps artillery is prepared to deliver) Tj
T*
(counter-battery fire on call. Higher intent is to secure the Leh axis, restore the integrity of) Tj
T*
(the line of actual control in the assigned area, and establish conditions for a follow-on) Tj
T*
(relief in place by 8 Mountain Division.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(c. Attachments and Detachments. Effective from 0300 hours on D-1, the mechanised infantry) Tj
T*
(battalion is attached to 14 Mountain Brigade. The combat engineer company reverts to divisional) Tj
T*
(control on completion of the breach and passage of lines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. MISSION.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(14 Mountain Brigade seizes and secures the dominating ground overlooking the northern) Tj
T*
(approaches to the Leh sector not later than 0600 hours on D-Day, in order to deny the enemy) Tj
T*
