(3. EXECUTION.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(a. Commander's Intent. My intent is to close with the enemy along the western valley while) Tj
T*
(fixing him in the east with deception and harassing fires. The decisive operation is the) Tj
T*
(seizure of Objective FALCON by the main effort; supporting operations isolate the objective and) Tj
T*
(secure the lines of communication. The end state is achieved when the dominating ground is) Tj
T*
(under our control, the main supply route is protected from direct fire and observation, and the) Tj
T*
(brigade is postured to hand over to the relieving formation without a pause in the defence.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(b. Concept of Operations. The operation is conducted in three phases. Phase One, shaping,) Tj
T*
(extends from D-2 to H-Hour and comprises reconnaissance, obstacle reduction, and the movement) Tj
T*
(of forces to attack positions under cover of darkness and electromagnetic emission control.) Tj
T*
(Phase Two, the decisive action, begins at H-Hour with a synchronised assault on Objective) Tj
T*
(FALCON supported by preparatory artillery fires and close air support on call. Phase Three,) Tj
T*
(consolidation, begins on seizure of the objective and includes reorganisation, casualty) Tj
T*
(evacuation, resupply, and preparation for the relief in place.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(c. Scheme of Manoeuvre. The main effort advances along the western axis with two assault) Tj
T*
(battalions forward and one in depth. The mechanised battalion conducts a supporting attack) Tj
T*
(along the eastern axis to fix the enemy and to protect the right flank. The reconnaissance) Tj
T*
(flight screens the northern approaches and provides early warning of any enemy repositioning.) Tj
T*
(Engineers reduce the linear obstacle at the valley mouth and mark two lanes for the passage of) Tj
T*
(the mechanised force.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(d. Fires. Priority of fires is to the main effort throughout. A programme of preparatory fires) Tj
T*
(strikes identified command posts, mortar positions, and anti-tank teams from H minus fifteen) Tj
T*
(minutes. Counter-battery fire is on call from corps artillery. Restrictions: no fires within) Tj
T*
(one thousand metres of the marked cultural site at grid reference sector nine; all requests) Tj
T*
(routed through the brigade fire support coordination cell.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(e. Coordinating Instructions. H-Hour is confirmed by codeword THUNDERBOLT transmitted on the) Tj
T*
(command net. Timings are relative to H-Hour unless stated otherwise. The rules of engagement in) Tj
T*
(force are those promulgated for the exercise and remain in effect until formally rescinded. All) Tj
T*
(units report crossing of phase lines using the designated checkpoints.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
