(4. SERVICE SUPPORT.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(a. Sustainment. The brigade maintenance area is established two kilometres south of the) Tj
T*
(assembly area. Combat supplies are pushed forward on a daily maintenance cycle; two days of) Tj
T*
(supply are held at unit level. Water is drawn from the divisional point and distributed by unit) Tj
T*
(transport. Ammunition resupply during the decisive action is by pre-positioned caches at the) Tj
T*
(attack positions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(b. Medical. The field surgical team is co-located with the brigade maintenance area. Casualty) Tj
T*
(evacuation is by ground ambulance to the collection point and thence by air to the divisional) Tj
T*
(hospital, weather permitting. Each battalion establishes a regimental aid post forward.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(c. Transport and Movement. Movement forward is by unit vehicles along the designated route,) Tj
T*
(staggered to preserve tactical dispersion. Traffic control points are manned by the provost) Tj
T*
(detachment from D-1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
