(5. COMMAND AND SIGNAL.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(a. Command. The brigade commander locates with the tactical headquarters on the western axis) Tj
T*
(during the decisive action. Succession of command is the deputy commander, then the commanding) Tj
T*
(officer of the leading assault battalion. Main headquarters remains in the assembly area.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(b. Signal. Primary means of communication is secure combat net radio; alternate is line to) Tj
T*
(fixed locations; contingency is dispatch rider; emergency is pyrotechnic signal per the signal) Tj
T*
(instruction. Electromagnetic emission control state is amber until H-Hour, thereafter green.) Tj
T*
(Codewords, nicknames, and the challenge and password for the period are issued separately under) Tj
T*
(the signal instruction.) Tj
T*
() Tj
